                "correctAnswerMessage": "Correct — the statement is false. Fulminant hepatic failure requires the absence of pre-existing liver disease. When a child with chronic Wilson disease decompensates, this is classified as acute-on-chronic liver failure, a distinct entity with different prognostic and management implications.",
